      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T15:03:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to IEEE 802.1AB Table 8-4, system capabilities bits 0 through 7 are transmitted in Octet 1, which is value[0]. Packing (value[0] \u003c\u003c 8) | value[1] puts Octet 1 into the high byte, so standard capabilities like Bridge and Router will fail to decode from real switches. Please fix the octet order in both parser and unit tests.\"",
      "revId": "5babdc71d285102d95704bf7e06a5c85fc300630",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26a96f97_d53cfc84",
        "filename": "src/nvidia-gpu/LldpFrame.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 356,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T08:51:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The order is correct as written, because IEEE 802.1AB-2016 section 8.1 makes the lower numbered octet the most significant one and section 8.4.3 makes bit 1 the least significant bit of the field, so bit 1 (Other) is the low bit of value[1], which is also how lldpd encodes it and Wireshark decodes it.",
      "parentUuid": "7537f3b6_c17881d5",
      "revId": "5babdc71d285102d95704bf7e06a5c85fc300630",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
